WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/features/analytics/components/analytics/BatteryTab.tsx — the analytics "Battery" tab:
    props: { data: FleetAnalytics | undefined }; reads useTranslation + useUnits (unitPrefs.distance,
    formatEnergy). trend = data?.battery_trend ?? []; latest = trend[trend.length - 1].
    BRANCHES:
      • trend.length === 0  ⇒ <GlassPanel><EmptyState message="No battery trend data available"
                              icon={<Battery/>} /></GlassPanel>
      • else (content)      ⇒ <FadeIn> 5 MetricCards + 4 charts:
          MetricCards: Health Score (fmtNumber(safe(health_score),1) %, Heart, green),
                       Capacity (formatEnergy(safe(capacity_wh),{precision:1}), Battery, cyan),
                       Degradation (fmtNumber(safe(degradation_pct),2) %, TrendingUp, amber),
                       Est. Range (fmtNumber(fromKm(safe(range_km)),0) <unit>, MapPin, purple),
                       Cycles (fmtInt(safe(cycle_count)), Activity, cyan).
          Charts:      Health Score Timeline — AreaChart, YAxis domain={[80,100]}, series "Health %".
                       Capacity Trend        — LineChart of capacity_wh (raw Wh).
                       Range Trend           — LineChart of fromKm(range_km), series "Range (<unit>)".
                       Degradation & Cycles  — ComposedChart: Area degradation_pct (yAxisId left) +
                                               Line cycle_count (yAxisId right) + <Legend/>.
          fromKm(km) = convertDistanceFromSI(km*1000, distanceUnit); x tick = date.slice(5) ("MM-DD").
  Loading / error / stale / offline are owned by the web parent page; this native surface re-homes
  them onto the shared P1/S8 source seam so every prompt-required state renders (same shape every P4 surface uses).

